  "extraction_notes": [
    "P-channel signs are preserved in tabulated electrical values: VGS, VDS, ID, and IS are negative as printed; resistance and capacitance values are positive. Curve points use positive magnitudes because the plotted axes are labeled -VDS, -VGS, -ID, or -IS.",
    "Electrical characteristics are specified at TA=25 \u00b0C unless otherwise stated. The 25 \u00b0C and 125 \u00b0C traces are retained separately where the figure labels them; Figures 1 and 3 and the capacitance figure do not state temperature in the plot.",
    "Figures 1-7 were examined. Curves are approximate digitizations of visible plotted traces, with only points read from the axes and traces retained. No curve points were interpolated beyond the plotted trace.",
    "The datasheet publishes typical CISS=1780 pF, COSS=235 pF, and CRSS=200 pF at VGS=0 V, VDS=-15 V, f=1 MHz; values are normalized to SI farads here.",
    "RDS(on) is published as typical and maximum at VGS=-10 V, ID=-12 A and at VGS=-4.5 V, ID=-7 A; all four rows are preserved.",
    "The datasheet publishes QG(TOT)=46 nC typical, QGS=1.0 nC typical, and QGD=1.4 nC typical at VGS=-10 V, VDS=-15 V, ID=-15 A. The strict schema has no gate-charge field, so these are noted but not represented as specs.",
    "The datasheet publishes Rg=6.0 ohm typical, switching times, gFS=40 S typical, and thermal resistances, but the strict schema has no fields for these quantities.",
    "No reverse-recovery time trr is published for the body diode. Avalanche energy is an absolute rating and is not treated as a fitted diode curve."
  ],
